      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "HTTP::Body versions before 1.24_01 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via regex backtracking on the filename of a multipart upload.\n\nFor every file part, the multipart parser finds the suffix of the uploaded filename by matching the default $basename_regexp, qr/[^.]+(\\.[^\\\\\\/]+)$/, against the whole basename. A basename made of many dots and ending in a backslash makes the regex backtrack in time quadratic in its length.\n\nA remote attacker can exhaust CPU with one request, as a basename of about 32 KB takes several seconds to match and every file part is matched separately.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
      "publisher": {
